# Suspension fits beautifully into this architecture

This also solves the requirement you just introduced.

Suppose:

```text
Admission Policy

REQUIRED:
    OfficerIdentityVerification
```

Voter:

```text
Registered
   ↓
Identity verified
   ↓
ADMITTED
   ↓
CAN VOTE
```

Now suspension:

```text
SUSPEND
   ↓
Voter remains registered
   ↓
Voting entitlement = FALSE
   ↓
RevalidationRequired
```

Then:

```text
Reverification
   ↓
New admission evidence
   ↓
Revalidation satisfied
   ↓
ADMITTED again
   ↓
CAN VOTE
```

Notice something important:

**Suspension is not another verification method.**

It is a **state transition that invalidates the current admission condition**.

That distinction will make the architecture much cleaner.

---

# I would therefore rename some concepts

Instead of:

```text
Gate 1
Gate 2
Gate 3
Gate 4
```

I recommend:

```text
Admission Requirement
Admission Evidence
Admission Decision
Revalidation Requirement
Voting Security Constraint
Voting Entitlement
```

Then specific requirements can be:

```text
OfficerIdentityVerification
EmailOwnershipVerification
PhoneOwnershipVerification
ElectronicIdentityVerification
OrganizationalApproval
```

And security constraints:

```text
IPNetworkConstraint
DeviceConstraint
SessionConstraint
```

And evidence:

```text
IdentityAttested
EmailOwnershipConfirmed
PhoneOwnershipConfirmed
OrganizationalApprovalRecorded
```

